# Artifacts and rich outputs

Small values move through `ctx`. Tables, reports, and other files move as
explicit cell outputs.

```python {#prepare independent=true}
ctx.records = [
    {"region": "north", "requests": 120, "latency_ms": 18.4},
    {"region": "south", "requests": 95, "latency_ms": 22.1},
    {"region": "west", "requests": 140, "latency_ms": 16.8},
]
ctx.total_requests = sum(row["requests"] for row in ctx.records)
print(f"Prepared {len(ctx.records)} regions")
```

```python {#publish depends-on=prepare}
display.csv(ctx.records, "metrics.csv")
display.markdown(
    f"## Service summary\n\nTotal requests: **{ctx.total_requests}**.",
    "summary.md",
)
```

```python {#manifest depends-on=publish}
import json

csv_file = outputs.path("publish", "metrics.csv")
summary_file = outputs.path("publish", "summary.md")
manifest = {
    "files": [csv_file.name, summary_file.name],
    "csv_bytes": csv_file.stat().st_size,
    "total_requests": ctx.total_requests,
}
output_path("manifest.json").write_text(
    json.dumps(manifest, indent=2, sort_keys=True),
    encoding="utf-8",
)
```

```python {#verify-artifacts role=test test-of=manifest}
import json

csv_text = outputs.path("publish", "metrics.csv").read_text(encoding="utf-8")
manifest = json.loads(outputs.path("manifest", "manifest.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
assert set(csv_text.splitlines()[0].split(",")) == {"region", "requests", "latency_ms"}
assert manifest["files"] == ["metrics.csv", "summary.md"]
assert manifest["total_requests"] == 355
```
